    ],
    comingSoon: false,
    minPlayers: 4,
    maxPlayers: 4,
    routePath: 'biritch',
    LLM: "Game: Biritch (1886 original Bridge). 4 players, partnerships. 52 cards, 13 each. Dealer declares trumps or 'biritch' (no-trump). Partner's hand exposed as Dummy. Contre/sur-contre doubles. 30 pts = game, best of 3 = rubber. Honours scored separately.",
    Player: "Constantinople, 1882. You hold: â™ AKQ73 â™¥J85 â™¦K92 â™£64. As dealer, you may declare trumps or pass to your partner. With 5 strong spades, you declare Spades. Your opponent contres! Do you sur-contre with your AKQ? Your partner's Dummy will be revealed after you decide...",
    tagline: 'Where Bridge began. Declare trumps, expose the Dummy, play the hand.',
    gameCategory: 'Trick-taking',
