          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Biritch (early bridge) with auction and contract play.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump and no-trump are determined by the auction; follow suit when able. Suit hierarchy for bidding: no-trump highest, then spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit (ace through two). Standard trick order; contract is set by the auction. Declarer and dummy play against the defenders; rank and trump order follow bridge conventions.',
