            title: 'BIRITCH',
            subtitle: 'The Original Bridge (1886)',
            tagline: 'Where Bridge began. Declare trumps, expose the Dummy, play the hand.',
          },
          shortDescription: "The ancestor of all Bridge games, first documented in 1886 by a British engineer who learned it from the Russian colony in Constantinople. The dealer declares trumps (or 'biritch' for no-trump), the partner's hand is exposed as Dummy, and the race to 30 points begins. Only three copies of the original rules survive.",
